items.brief:
Turn bindings into a table. Merge this item FIRST in batch 1 (plan 0.2).

1. Create the pure, edge-safe lib/registry/sources.js. It is imported by lib/registry/index.js, which 'use client' editor modules import, so it ships to the browser: it may import only pure modules under lib/registry/ (no lib/db, lib/repo, lib/catalog, lib/commerce, lib/offers, lib/cms, next/*, node:). Resolvers only call the injected repo and ctx.
   Exports: SOURCES (name -> { args, resolve(repo, args, ctx), prefetch?(argsList, repo, ctx), argOf?(settingValue) }), getSource(name), and the test seams defineSource(decl) and removeSource(name).
   Declare six sources:
   - featured_collections (curated slice or repo.getFeaturedCollections);
   - newest_products;
   - collection_products (railProducts, with documents pins vs legacy pins);
   - route_product (known, no home data: resolves to undefined, never logs);
   - bundle_by_id: argOf { id } -> id; resolve returns the bundle entry from the prefetched Map (undefined when absent; the component treats that as missing);
   - bundles_by_ids: argOf [{ id }] -> ids (order kept); resolve returns the entries in the picked order, skipping none (absent ids give { id, state: 'missing' }).
   The two bundle sources share one prefetch that gathers every bundle id across all instances of both sources (dedupe) into ONE repo.bundlesByIds(ids) call. A rejected prefetch rejects every bundle instance (bindingFailed path). No kind uses the bundle sources until P5-BLOCKS, and repo.bundlesByIds is wired into DEFAULT_REPO there, not here.
   Move the existing resolver bodies out of the if/else in lib/cms/section-data.js run(). The collection argOf replaces the special case in argOf() for { handle, id } -> handle. The curated and pins pre-reads stay as they are; expose them to resolvers through ctx.
2. lib/registry/index.js:
   - defineSection normalises a singular `source` to `sources`, checks each binding is { sources: [nonEmpty strings], args: [keys of its settings] }, and throws when a source is not in SOURCES.
   - checkRegistry() reports every kind whose binding names a source no longer in SOURCES (so a removeSource after registration is caught).
3. lib/cms/section-data.js run(): look the source up in the table. Unknown -> a rejected promise with an Error whose code is 'source_unknown'. The existing catch adds the field to data.bindingFailed and logs slog section_binding_failed with a new cause field ('source_unknown' or 'fault'). Also set data.bindingFailedCause = { [field]: cause } (P5-HIDDEN reads it to pick the preview words). Run each source's prefetch once, with every instance's args, before the per-instance loop. Keep the queryCache key and the limit default (Number(limit) || defaults.limit || 8) exactly as they are for the existing sources.
4. lib/registry/validate.js: an instance section.bindings source not in SOURCES is also BINDING_INVALID (guard the existing declared.sources.includes against a declaration without sources). New BINDING_INVALID message, matching the removeSection action checks.js already offers for it: "This <label> section is set up in a way the editor can't fix. Remove it and add it again." Update any test that pins the old wording.
5. package.json (the only package.json edit in phase 5): register test:commerce-blocks -> node scripts/test-commerce-blocks.js and test:bundle-form -> node scripts/test-bundle-form.js. Create both files as passing placeholders that print 'placeholder: filled by P5-BLOCKS' / 'placeholder: filled by P5-PANEL'. The gate goes from 96 to 98 suites.
6. scripts/test-sections.js tests:
   - a throwaway source (defineSource) plus a throwaway kind resolves through resolveHomeSectionData with no other file changed; removeSource restores the table;
   - defineSection refuses an unknown source; checkRegistry reports a source removed after registration;
   - runtime: a source removed after registration gives bindingFailed [field], bindingFailedCause source_unknown, one section_binding_failed log with cause source_unknown, no collections, no throw. This is the ONLY proof of the runtime path (a draft cannot hold an unknown body binding: the writer refuses it);
   - registry-shaped sections ({ id, kind, settings }): collections at limits 3 and 6 and two `new` instances resolve independently, identical queries made once;
   - bundle sources with a fake repo: 2 bundle_by_id instances and 1 bundles_by_ids instance of 4 make exactly one repo.bundlesByIds call with the 5 to 6 deduped ids; order kept; a rejecting fake gives bindingFailed (cause fault) on all three;
   - route_product: no data, no log;
   - an import scan: lib/registry/sources.js imports only lib/registry/* pure modules (none of lib/db, lib/repo, lib/catalog, lib/commerce, lib/offers, lib/cms, node:);
   - a body key scan over section SETTINGS only: every registry default, every SETTING_KINDS empty() value, the starter bodies, and the worst-case SECTION SETTINGS in lib/registry/fixtures.js (not its render data, which legitimately carries soldOut) contain no key price, compare_at_price, bundle_price, inventory, total_inventory, available, sold_out or soldOut. seed-design-documents bodies need a database and are not scanned; P5-SETTING's structural UNKNOWN_FIELD test carries that guarantee.

The unknown-body-binding validator case already exists (test-registry-contract.js about line 1098, source 'every_product'); this item does not edit test-registry-contract.js (P5-SETTING owns it in batch 1, P5-BLOCKS adds the explicit checkRegistry negative there in batch 2).

Legacy: lib/cms/registry.js and componentFor stay untouched; legacy declarations (singular source) resolve through the same table. The a6d028e home-render fixtures and test-release-readers v1 to v4 stay byte-identical.

Give the founder a reason in preview for a section, or a part of one, that hides itself, without changing live markup.

1. components/sections/index.js:
   - an optional static component hook hiddenReason(section, data, ctx) -> string | null;
   - export hiddenNote(section, data, ctx): returns the founder note element only in a documents preview and only when the component declares hiddenReason and it returns text; otherwise null. The note uses the existing founder-note look (unfinished / failed notes), carries data-sec from ctx.secKey (as SectionView does) so click-to-select works, and data-hidden-reason;
   - export isFounderPreview(ctx) and a FounderNote part (or put it in parts.js) so a component can render a per-cell note in preview (P5-BLOCKS uses it for dropped grid cells);
   - the bindingFailed preview note reads data.bindingFailedCause (set by P5-SOURCES): cause source_unknown says 'This section is set up in a way the editor can't fix. Remove it and add it again.'; a fault keeps 'Reload the preview to try again'. Missing cause = today's text.
2. components/sections/HomeSections.js: where !sectionShows(s, data) returns null, return hiddenNote(s, data, ctxFor(s)) instead, building ctx with secKey the same way SectionView gets it. Shoppers still get null. A hidden note never counts as a shown section for the #new anchor; it counts towards emptyNote in preview only. First find and record in the packet how the documents preview is detected today (inDocumentsPreview() or the flag the preview route sets) and use exactly that signal; legacy previews must not trigger it.
3. Only kinds whose component declares hiddenReason are affected. No existing component gets the hook, so product_rail (PV-09, P1) and all live pages are unchanged.
4. scripts/test-sections-render.js: use the existing registerSectionComponent seam (index.js about line 61) with a throwaway kind. Test that:
   - a hidden section with hiddenReason renders the note in a documents preview render (through the same preview signal the preview route sets) with data-sec and data-hidden-reason, and nothing live;
   - a kind without the hook renders nothing in both;
   - a bindingFailed section with cause source_unknown shows the remove words in preview, and with cause fault the reload words;
   - live home markup for the worst-case and a6d028e fixtures is byte-identical before and after.

HOME_EMPTY is unaffected (it counts enabled body sections, not rendered ones). No legacy impact.

Add bundle publish warnings that never block, and prove the BINDING_INVALID remove path.

1. lib/documents/checks.js referenceChecks:
   - Collect every { ref: 'bundle', id } from refsOf(section) across the document (settings only; /bundles/<slug> links are not checked in phase 5, a recorded known limit).
   - When the document has no bundle ref, make NO bundle statement (existing statement-count tests in test-publish-checks and test-publish-service must not move). Otherwise read them with ONE guarded bundlesByIds(ids) call (lib/commerce/bundle-read.js), at most 3 statements whatever the number of refs. A read failure gives the existing 'checks could not run' handling, never a false missing.
   - Warnings (text from lib/commerce/bundle-words.js, naming the bundle title or the id when gone):
     - BUNDLE_MISSING (deleted);
     - BUNDLE_DISABLED (turned off);
     - BUNDLE_UNAVAILABLE (sold_out, no_saving, not_ready; says shoppers see 'Currently unavailable', and for no_saving gives the live component sum through formatMoney(sum, currency ?? undefined) and says to lower the price in Catalog > Bundles);
     - BUNDLE_OVERLAP (a picked, enabled bundle shares a product with another enabled bundle: 'Another bundle uses the same products, so the cart may give a different saving than this block shows.'). Not removable; openField.
   - BUNDLE_MISSING, BUNDLE_DISABLED and BUNDLE_UNAVAILABLE go in REMOVABLE_WARNINGS: decorate() gives removeSection for a card's bundle setting and removeItem (that index only) for a bundle_list entry. The button words come from components/admin/editor/publish/publishModel.js actionLabel, which is not changed in phase 5: removeSection reads 'Remove this section and publish' and removeItem 'Remove it and publish'; the warning message itself names what goes (for a grid entry: 'Remove this bundle from the grid' is said in the message text, not the button). None is in publish.js STRUCTURE_CODES.
2. scripts/test-publish-checks.js: register a throwaway kind with a bundle setting and a bundle_list setting (defineSection plus removeSection), because the real kinds land in P5-BLOCKS in the same batch. Seed with lib/bundles.js createBundle / setBundleEnabled / deleteBundle on a tenant-fixture file DB; plant a sold-out variant through the sync writer (tenant-fixture's writeProduct path, availableForSale false). Assert:
   - BUNDLE_MISSING on the card with removeSection, and replaying it removes the section;
   - BUNDLE_MISSING on ONE bundle_list entry with removeItem for that index only (the grid half of the missing cell);
   - BUNDLE_DISABLED on a bundle_list entry with removeItem for that index only;
   - BUNDLE_UNAVAILABLE for a sold-out component ('Currently unavailable') and for no_saving (names the sum);
   - BUNDLE_OVERLAP for two overlapping enabled bundles, with openField only;
   - publishing a document carrying all four succeeds (follow the existing PRODUCT_UNAVAILABLE pattern for any acknowledgement the publish flow needs);
   - a faulting read gives no BUNDLE_MISSING and the existing checks-failed handling;
   - the bundle checks use the same statement count (at most 3, warm probe) for 1 and for 12 refs;
   - BINDING_INVALID remove path (TREE-01, from review): a draft holding an instance binding with source 'no_such_source', written straight into the test DB (the writer refuses it, so this is a named test-only plant), gets BINDING_INVALID with the 'Remove it and add it again' message and a removeSection action; replaying the action clears the issue and publish succeeds.

No legacy impact: checks run only on documents publish.

Owner answers (2026-11-05): OQ-B is answered AGAINST the default: a bundle whose price no longer saves anything (no_saving) is HIDDEN for shoppers, like disabled: the card is hidden and a grid drops its cell; the founder sees a note with the reason in preview and the inspector; publish still warns BUNDLE_UNAVAILABLE (non-blocking, names the sum). The no_saving words become: 'The price no longer saves anything (the products add up to <sum>), so shoppers don't see it. Lower the price in Catalog > Bundles.' sold_out and not_ready are unchanged ('Currently unavailable', add off). OQ-C: inline create turns the bundle on at once (default kept). Deviation 3.10 (bundle API changes) is accepted.
For no_saving, BUNDLE_UNAVAILABLE's message says shoppers don't see the block (not 'Currently unavailable') and still names the sum.
